From my understanding of the problem, only the pum area is updated while its active.  When the buffer horizontally scrolls, the pum's area is changed, but nothing is done to restore the cells under the old area.  This is what I came up with to fix it:

```diff
diff --git a/src/nvim/edit.c b/src/nvim/edit.c
index ecc794f..59927cf 100644
--- a/src/nvim/edit.c
+++ b/src/nvim/edit.c
@@ -4334,6 +4334,14 @@ static int ins_complete(int c, bool enable_pum)
   int n;
   int save_w_wrow;
   int insert_match;
+  static win_T *lastwin = NULL;
+  static colnr_T lastcol = 0;
+
+  if (lastwin != curwin) {
+    lastwin = curwin;
+    lastcol = curwin->w_leftcol;
+  }
+
 
   compl_direction = ins_compl_key2dir(c);
   insert_match = ins_compl_use_match(c);
@@ -4821,6 +4829,11 @@ static int ins_complete(int c, bool enable_pum)
   compl_was_interrupted = compl_interrupted;
   compl_interrupted = FALSE;
 
+  if (lastcol != curwin->w_leftcol) {
+    redraw_later(CLEAR);
+    lastcol = curwin->w_leftcol;
+  }
+
   return OK;
 }
 ```

![compl](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/111942/23439666/c07db298-fde5-11e6-99b8-9319becf3532.gif)

It's a little heavy handed with the `CLEAR`, but I don't think anyone would consider long completions or tiny windows to be normal enough for it to matter.

Is there a better way of keeping track of the last `w_leftcol`?
